concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372ja a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "372JA Remedial notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-372ja ;
    values:originalText "Scope (1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a person: (a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or (b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in circumstances that make it likely that the contravention will continue or be repeated; or (c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision. Note: For designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH. Remedial notice (2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the person to: (a) remedy the contravention; or (b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or (c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or likely contravention. (3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice.  Deployment of optical fibre  Schedule 2  No. 36, 2024 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer Safeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024" ;
    skos:definition "Scope (1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a person: (a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or (b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in circumstances that make it likely that the contravention will continue or be repeated; or (c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision. Note: For designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH. Remedial notice (2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the person to: (a) remedy the contravention; or (b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or (c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or likely contravention. (3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice.  Deployment of optical fibre  Schedule 2  No. 36, 2024 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer Safeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372ja-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372ja-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372ja-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2024a00036.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2024a00036.pdf, p.70" .
doc:sch-2-sec-372ja a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "372JA Remedial notices" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Scope (1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a person: (a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or (b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in circumstances that make it likely that the contravention will continue or be repeated; or (c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision. Note: For designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH. Remedial notice (2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the person to: (a) remedy the contravention; or (b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or (c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or likely contravention. (3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice.  Deployment of optical fibre  Schedule 2  No. 36, 2024 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer Safeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024" ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer .

