concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "372JC Compliance with remedial notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-372jc ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must comply with a remedial notice. Ancillary contraventions (2) A person must not: (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of subsection (1); or (b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a contravention of subsection (1); or  Schedule 2  Deployment of optical fibre  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer Safeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024 No. 36, 2024 (c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or (d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of subsection (1). Civil penalty provisions (3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must comply with a remedial notice. Ancillary contraventions (2) A person must not: (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of subsection (1); or (b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a contravention of subsection (1); or  Schedule 2  Deployment of optical fibre  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer Safeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024 No. 36, 2024 (c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or (d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of subsection (1). Civil penalty provisions (3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions."@en ;
